# libFuzzer-generated corpus entries (SHA-1 hex names). Reproducible
# named seeds are tracked; the hex-named files below are run artifacts
# and grow without bound.
fuzz/corpus/*/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]

# libFuzzer diagnostic dumps written at the CWD (slow inputs, crash inputs,
# OOM inputs, timeout inputs). Reproducible cases graduate into
# `fuzz/corpus/`; these root-level dumps are transient run artifacts.
slow-unit-*
crash-*
oom-*
timeout-*
leak-*

# Audit / analysis scratch. The canonical security invariants live at
# `docs/security-invariants.md`; ad-hoc audit dumps at the repo root
# should not be committed.
/PRODUCTION_READINESS_AUDIT.md
/SECURITY_AUDIT_*.md
/SECURITY_AUDIT_*.html
/analysis.md
/analysis.html
/catapult_analysis.md
/catapult_analysis.html